## Summary

Delivered a native **SwiftUI / Apple HIG** implementation of the web `CostAnalysisPage` (route `/charging/costs`, alias `/cost-analysis`) at full parity, adaptive across macOS + iOS.

**Path note (no silent drift):** the prompt's `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Charging/**` is not a compiled source root; per the Powershare precedent I implemented under the real compiled path `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Charging/**` — verified by both builds compiling all 12 files.

**What shipped (19 files, +4520 lines, commit `ce24a20a9`):**
- 12 source files + 1 test file: `@Observable CostAnalysisPageModel` over a `CostAnalysisDataSource` seam (web hooks `useChargingSessionsPaginated` + `useCostForecast` kept at call sites); a pure economics pipeline mirroring `useCostAnalysisData`.
- **No scope narrowing** — every web region reproduced natively: 6 summary cards, monthly-cost area chart, cost-per-kWh line chart, charger-type pie + bars, gas-vs-EV savings calculator (3 live inputs + 4 tiles + reset), sortable monthly table, time-of-use bars + insights, AI-narration slot, cost-forecast section (forecast chart + breakdown donut + savings + insights + trend), lifetime summary, environmental impact — each with loading/empty/success/error states on the P3 Swift Charts wrappers.
- SI discipline: SI stored (Wh/W/m), display conversion only at the boundary via `Units`.
- Wiring: `AppRoute.costAnalysis` + parser aliases + app registry; 105 string-catalog keys (additions-only); ledger rows (macos+ios, 7/7 done).

**Gate — all green:**
| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| swiftlint --strict | 0 violations (6122 files) |
| placeholder scan | 0 (2 documented redaction markers) |
| macOS build | ✅ SUCCEEDED (12 files compiled) |
| iOS arm64-sim build | ✅ SUCCEEDED (`#if os(iOS)` branches) |
| CostAnalysisPageModelTests | ✅ 20/20 passed |
| PARITY | 7/7 (3 states + 4 strings) |

Pre-existing, out-of-scope Xcode-26.5 incompatibilities (`Input.Previews.swift`, `GDPR/Timeline/VehicleCost…Tests.swift`, and the framework's missing x86_64-sim slice) were isolated via build settings only and fully disclosed in the evidence log — `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`.

